<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕlōrus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i,
		m., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕlōrum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέλωρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a promontory on the
				north-eastern coast of Sicily</i>, the modern <i>Capo di Faro</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Peloros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 727</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pelorus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 78</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pelorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 10, § 73</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6, §
			646</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕ-lōrĭtānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Pelorian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
